[{"category":"section","location":"reference/#Reference","page":"Reference","text":"","title":"Reference"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.AbstractBilinearFormNetwork","page":"Reference","text":"abstract type AbstractBilinearFormNetwork{T, V, I} <: AbstractITensorNetwork{T, V}\n\nSupertype of the lazy multi-layer networks built from a ket layer of type ITensorNetwork{T, V, I} and a ket→bra index name mapping.\n\nA subtype supplies its own graph structure and implements braname together with one accessor per layer: kettensor, bratensor and, where the subtype has an operator layer, operatortensor. bratensor has a default built from kettensor and braname.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.AbstractBilinearFormNetwork"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.AbstractBilinearFormNetworkView","page":"Reference","text":"abstract type AbstractBilinearFormNetworkView{T, V, I} <: AbstractITensorNetwork{T, V}\n\nSupertype of the single-layer views of an AbstractBilinearFormNetwork{T, V, I}.\n\nA subtype implements Base.parent, returning the network it views, and DataGraphs.get_vertex_data, returning that layer's tensor at a vertex. Its graph structure and mutability are those of the parent network.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.AbstractBilinearFormNetworkView"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.ITensorNetworkOperator","page":"Reference","text":"struct ITensorNetworkOperator{T, V, I, P} <: AbstractITensorNetwork{T, V}\n\nThe network equivalent of ITensorBase.ITensorOperator: a tensor network of type P <: AbstractITensorNetwork{T, V} together with a pairing of its dangling index names, where outputnames[i] is paired with inputnames[i]. Applying the operator contracts over the input names and leaves the output names.\n\nA pair may straddle two vertices, as it does for a swap or a translation. Indexing returns the vertex tensor wrapped as an ITensorOperator carrying only the pairs whose two halves both sit on that vertex; the remaining legs are dangling on the wrapper.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.ITensorNetworkOperator"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.NormNetwork","page":"Reference","text":"struct NormNetwork{T, V, I} <: AbstractBilinearFormNetwork{T, V, I}\n\nLazy wrapper representing the norm ⟨tn|tn⟩ of tn::ITensorNetwork{T, V, I}, together with a per-edge ket→bra name mapping that, for each index in the ket layer, defines the name of the corresponding index in the bra layer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.NormNetwork"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.QuadraticFormNetwork","page":"Reference","text":"struct QuadraticFormNetwork{T, V, I, O} <: AbstractBilinearFormNetwork{T, V, I}\n\nLazy wrapper representing the quadratic form ⟨tn|op|tn⟩ of tn::ITensorNetwork{T, V, I} sandwiched around the operator layer op::ITensorNetworkOperator, together with a per-index ket→bra name mapping that, for each index in the ket layer, defines the name of the corresponding index in the bra layer.\n\nThe operator layer must be defined on every vertex of tn. Its input names are ket index names, and each paired output name is renamed to the bra layer, so the operator's remaining index names must be distinct from every index name of tn.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.QuadraticFormNetwork"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.apply_operator-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"apply_operator(operator, state, env; alg=nothing, kwargs...) -> (state, env)\n\nApply a single operator to state and return an updated (state, env) pair. Environments are not fully recomputed; only the edges touched by operator are updated (for a two-site gate, the BP simple-update default writes new messages on the gate edge). For the BP simple-update default algorithm, kwargs accept trunc (forwarded to the SVD that splits the gate back into single-site tensors) and normalize (whether to rescale the post-gate state so the singular-value spectrum stays unit-norm).\n\nSee also apply_operators.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.apply_operator"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.apply_operators-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"apply_operators(operators, state, env; alg=nothing, kwargs...) -> (state, env)\n\nApply each operator in operators (a sequence of single-tensor or two-tensor operators) to state in turn, updating env to reflect each application. state is an AbstractITensorNetwork, env is a per-edge environment cache (typically built by identity_norm_message_env(state) or one of the related *_norm_message_env constructors), and the returned (state, env) pair has the operators applied. kwargs are forwarded to the per-operator algorithm (alg); for the default BP simple-update algorithm these include trunc (forwarded to the SVD that splits a two-site gate back into single-site tensors) and normalize.\n\nSee also apply_operator.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.apply_operators"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.beliefpropagation-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"beliefpropagation(factors, messages; edges, stopping_criterion, message_update_algorithm) -> MessageCache\n\nRun belief propagation on the factor graph factors, starting from messages (a dictionary keyed by directed edges). Returns the converged MessageCache. edges is the sweep schedule (defaults to a forest-cover edge sequence). stopping_criterion is required and accepts a NamedTuple shorthand ((; maxiter), (; tol), (; maxiter, tol)) or an explicit AlgorithmsInterface.StoppingCriterion. message_update_algorithm controls how a single message is recomputed from its incoming neighbours.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.beliefpropagation"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.braname","page":"Reference","text":"braname(bn::AbstractBilinearFormNetwork, name)\n\nThe bra-layer index name corresponding to the ket-layer index name name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.braname"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.bratensor-Tuple{ITensorNetworksNext.AbstractBilinearFormNetwork, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"bratensor(bn::AbstractBilinearFormNetwork, vertex)\n\nThe bra-layer tensor at vertex.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.bratensor"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.kettensor","page":"Reference","text":"kettensor(bn::AbstractBilinearFormNetwork, vertex)\n\nThe ket-layer tensor at vertex.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.kettensor"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.normnetwork-Tuple{ITensorNetworksNext.ITensorNetwork}","page":"Reference","text":"normnetwork(tn::ITensorNetwork, [braname]) -> NormNetwork\n\nBuild the double-layer norm network ⟨tn|tn⟩, represented lazily as a NomnNetwork object. The optional second argument braname should implement braname[ketdimname] = bradimname for every link dimension name ketdimname in tn. If this is not specified, then a name is generated via the ITensorBase.uniquename function.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.normnetwork"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.operatortensor","page":"Reference","text":"operatortensor(bn::AbstractBilinearFormNetwork, vertex)\n\nThe operator-layer tensor at vertex, with its index names renamed so that its input legs meet the ket layer and its output legs meet the bra layer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.operatortensor"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.quadraticformnetwork-Tuple{ITensorNetworksNext.ITensorNetwork, ITensorNetworksNext.ITensorNetworkOperator}","page":"Reference","text":"quadraticformnetwork(tn::ITensorNetwork, op::ITensorNetworkOperator, [braname])\n\nBuild the triple-layer network ⟨tn|op|tn⟩, represented lazily as a QuadraticFormNetwork object. The optional third argument braname should implement braname[ketdimname] = bradimname for every link dimension name ketdimname in tn and every dimension name of tn the operator acts on. If this is not specified, then a name is generated via the ITensorBase.uniquename function.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.quadraticformnetwork"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.ITensorNetworkGenerators.delta_network-Tuple{Any, Type, Graphs.AbstractGraph}","page":"Reference","text":"delta_network(f, elt::Type = Float64, g::AbstractGraph)\n\nConstruct a ITensorNetwork on the graph g with element type elt that has delta tensors on each vertex. Link dimensions are defined using the function f(e) that should take an edge e as an input and should output the link index on that edge.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.ITensorNetworkGenerators.delta_network"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#ITensorNetworksNext.ITensorNetworkGenerators.ising_network-Tuple{Any, Number, Graphs.AbstractGraph}","page":"Reference","text":"ising_network(f, β::Number, g::AbstractGraph)\n\nConstruct a ITensorNetwork on the graph g with inverse temperature β that has Ising partition function tensors on each vertex. Link dimensions are defined using the function f(e) that should take an edge e as an input and should output the link index on that edge.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.ITensorNetworkGenerators.ising_network"},{"category":"section","location":"#ITensorNetworksNext.jl","page":"Home","text":"(Image: Stable) (Image: Dev) (Image: Build Status) (Image: Coverage) (Image: Code Style) (Image: Aqua)","title":"ITensorNetworksNext.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Support","page":"Home","text":"<img class=\"display-light-only\" src=\"assets/CCQ.png\" width=\"20%\" alt=\"Flatiron Center for Computational Quantum Physics logo.\"/>\n<img class=\"display-dark-only\" src=\"assets/CCQ-dark.png\" width=\"20%\" alt=\"Flatiron Center for Computational Quantum Physics logo.\"/>\n\nITensorNetworksNext.jl is supported by the Flatiron Institute, a division of the Simons Foundation.","title":"Support"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation-instructions","page":"Home","text":"This package resides in the ITensor/ITensorRegistry local registry. In order to install, simply add that registry through your package manager. This step is only required once.\n\njulia> using Pkg: Pkg\n\njulia> Pkg.Registry.add(url=\"https://github.com/ITensor/ITensorRegistry\")\n\nor:\n\njulia> Pkg.Registry.add(url=\"git@github.com:ITensor/ITensorRegistry.git\")\n\nif you want to use SSH credentials, which can make it so you don't have to enter your Github ursername and password when registering packages.\n\nThen, the package can be added as usual through the package manager:\n\njulia> Pkg.add(\"ITensorNetworksNext\")","title":"Installation instructions"},{"category":"section","location":"#Examples","page":"Home","text":"using ITensorNetworksNext: ITensorNetworksNext\n\nExamples go here.\n\n\n\nThis page was generated using Literate.jl.","title":"Examples"}]
